## Freeze backend cards in view mode

Context: Domain → Information backend cards used hidden radio inputs. The
generic read-only CSS blocked pointer events on those inputs, but their labels
could still activate them and keyboard navigation could still change the
selected backend. Viewers and edit-locked users must not be able to alter this
domain setting.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
   Natively disables backend card radios for read-only versions, viewer roles,
   and edit locks; resynchronizes after lifecycle evaluation and whenever body
   permission classes change.
2. tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py
   Added regression contracts covering all three view-only states and
   mid-session permission changes.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
- tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-31.log

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 5739 passed, 305 skipped, 6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings in 51.73s.

Browser verification: `.role-viewer`, `.read-only-version`, and
`.read-only-locked` all natively disabled the four backend radios; pointer and
keyboard selection remained frozen, while removing the view-only state restored
interaction.

## Match Domain Information tab surface

Context: Domain → Information used a standalone bordered tab-content surface,
while the requested Ontology → Data Quality reference places its tab rail and
content inside one card. The separate surfaces produced different visible
borders, radii, spacing, and rail edges despite sharing the same tab component.

Changes:

